We recently updated from torch 2.7.1 to torch 2.9.0 and saw 15-20% performance regression on MPS. Bisecting torch revealed that #152515 introduced this regression, which landed in torch 2.8.0. There's no mention of this regression in the release notes https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/releases/tag/v2.8.0 and I can't find any other tickets tracking this.

Note that testing with a large dataset produced identical output when using 2.7.1 and 2.9.0, so the additional precision isn't required in our use case and hence it would be useful if we could opt-in to the old approach. For now we're using the following patch which restores the performance:
